  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Medline Industries has $91.3M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Medline Industries received 104 awards in FY2027 to date, with an average award size of $878K, and obligations are down 90.7% year over year. Annual obligations rose from FY22 through FY26 before the current-year reduction. Fiscal-year obligations were FY22 $281M, FY23 $337M, FY24 $370M, FY25 $579M, FY26 $987M, and FY27 $91.3M. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $89.1M. The Department of Justice is also a buyer, obligating $2.2M in FY2027 to date. Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the top NAICS market for Medline Industries in FY2027 to date at $90.8M. Medline Industries also has obligations in Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing at $573K and in General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $10K for FY2027 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Medline Industries’ FY2027 obligations?",
        "body": "Medline Industries’s FY2027 obligations concentrate with the Department of Veterans Affairs obligating $89.1M of the $91.3M total. Medline Industries’s top NAICS market, Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers, accounts for $90.8M of FY2027 obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 compare to prior fiscal years for Medline Industries?",
        "body": "Medline Industries’s obligations increased each year from FY22 through FY26 then declined in FY2027 to date: FY22 $281M, FY23 $337M, FY24 $370M, FY25 $579M, FY26 $987M, FY27 $91.3M. Medline Industries’s obligations are down 90.7% year over year in FY2027 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
